# Citation metadata of this repository (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub reads it for the "Cite this repository" button;
# the README section "Citation" gives the same reference in BibTeX. Keep the two in step.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below. If you use the data, also cite the DoS/DDoS-MQTT-IoT dataset paper."
type: software
title: "Privacy-Preserving Federated Synthetic Data Generation for Intrusion Detection in MQTT-Based IoT Gateways"
abstract: >-
  Code, configurations and results of PP-FedData, a study of privacy-preserving federated synthetic data generation for an
  intrusion detection system on the DoS/DDoS-MQTT-IoT dataset. It compares a CVAE trained by FedAvg with DP-SGD, SecAgg+ or
  both, and FedDP-Marginal, a generator built from per-class tables that the clients noise with their share of DP noise and
  sum by secure aggregation, against baselines trained on real data.
